uClibc-ng 1.0.59, include/features.h: restore the 1.0.54 conditional
_FILE_OFFSET_BITS behaviour (the Option-C edit).

Upstream 1.0.59 forced _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 for every consumer of
these headers, renaming the plain file calls to their *64 forms.
The programs this toolchain builds run against the hub's vendor
uClibc 0.9.30.3, which serves the plain entry points but never
exported getrlimit64, setrlimit64, lstat64, lockf64, mkstemp64,
mmap64 or freopen64 - every rebuilt program importing one of those
names dies at load time on the hub. This library's own runtime
does not bind the vendor runtime, so upstream's support policy
for its own libc does not apply here: the *64 interface applies
only when a program defines _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 itself.
build-toolchain.sh asserts the patched state survives into the
installed sysroot header, and apply-patches.sh verifies it in the
source copy before every build.

Provenance: commit f808564 ("uClibc-ng headers: make 64-bit file
offsets opt-in again").

--- a/include/features.h
+++ b/include/features.h
@@ -340,12 +340,19 @@
 # define __USE_LARGEFILE64	1
 #endif
 
-#if defined _FILE_OFFSET_BITS && _FILE_OFFSET_BITS != 64
-# error "_FILE_OFFSET_BITS != 64 is not supported by uClibc-ng"
+/* Sengled: upstream 1.0.59 forced _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 here for every
+   consumer of these headers. The programs this toolchain builds run
+   against the hub's vendor uClibc 0.9.30.3, which serves the plain
+   entry points but never exported getrlimit64, setrlimit64, lstat64,
+   lockf64, mkstemp64, mmap64 or freopen64 - so the 1.0.54 conditional
+   is restored: the *64 interface applies only when a program asks
+   for it itself. This library never ships (only its headers reach
+   consumer builds), so upstream's support policy for its own libc
+   does not bind the vendor runtime. build-toolchain.sh asserts this
+   edit survives into the installed sysroot header. */
+#if defined _FILE_OFFSET_BITS && _FILE_OFFSET_BITS == 64
+# define __USE_FILE_OFFSET64	1
 #endif
-#undef  _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
-#define _FILE_OFFSET_BITS	64
-#define __USE_FILE_OFFSET64	1
 
 #if defined _BSD_SOURCE || defined _SVID_SOURCE
 # define __USE_MISC	1
